---
export const title = 'Groups';
export const order = 250;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  <code>group-by</code> names a resource field, such as <code>team</code> or <code>floor</code>, to group the rows by.
  Groups keep the order they first appear in, a group's rows keep their order, and resources without the field form
  an "(Empty)" group. Each group starts with a header row showing its name and number of resources, and the header's
  button collapses or expands it.
</p>

<p>
  <code>group-toggle</code> fires with <code>&#123; group, expanded &#125;</code>, and <code>collapsed-groups</code>
  holds the keys of the collapsed groups (their values as strings, <code>""</code> for the empty group). Set it to
  start groups collapsed or to remember them between visits, as with <code>wc-table</code>'s groups. A collapsed
  group's header shows its events as thin bars, darker where they overlap, so you can see when it is busy without
  opening it. Events can be dragged between rows of different groups.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-calendar-timeline
    id='teams-timeline'
    resource-label='People'
    group-by='team'
    collapsed-groups='["Support"]'
    editable
    style='height: 420px; width: 100%'
  ></wc-calendar-timeline>
  <script is:inline>
    (function() {
      const $timeline = document.getElementById('teams-timeline');

      const today = new Date();
      today.setHours(0, 0, 0, 0);

      function at(hours, minutes) {
        const result = new Date(today);
        result.setHours(hours, minutes || 0, 0, 0);
        return result;
      }

      $timeline.resources = [
        { id: 'priya', title: 'Priya Natarajan', supportingText: 'Lead', team: 'Design' },
        { id: 'tomas', title: 'Tomás Ruiz', supportingText: 'Backend', team: 'Engineering' },
        { id: 'jo', title: 'Jo Park', supportingText: 'Researcher', team: 'Design' },
        { id: 'sam', title: 'Sam Okafor', supportingText: 'Frontend', team: 'Engineering' },
        { id: 'mei', title: 'Mei Chen', supportingText: 'Tier 2', team: 'Support' },
        { id: 'lea', title: 'Léa Martin', supportingText: 'Tier 1', team: 'Support' },
      ];

      $timeline.events = [
        { resourceId: 'priya', title: 'Design critique', start: at(10), end: at(11, 30), color: 'red' },
        { resourceId: 'jo', title: 'User interviews', start: at(13), end: at(16), color: 'orange' },
        { resourceId: 'tomas', title: 'Incident review', start: at(9), end: at(10), color: 'blue' },
        { resourceId: 'sam', title: 'Pairing', start: at(14), end: at(17), color: 'blue' },
        { resourceId: 'mei', title: 'Morning shift', start: at(7), end: at(15), color: 'green' },
        { resourceId: 'lea', title: 'Late shift', start: at(12), end: at(20), color: 'green' },
      ];

      $timeline.addEventListener('group-toggle', function(evt) {
        console.log('Group', evt.detail.group, evt.detail.expanded ? 'expanded' : 'collapsed');
      });
    })();
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>
